---
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What Cloud Peptides collects, how it's used, and how to contact us about your data."
  lastUpdated="August 8, 2026"
>
  <p class="cp-policy-note">
    <strong>Note:</strong> Cloud Peptides is an operating name, not a claim about a specific registered
    business entity or jurisdiction. This policy describes our actual current data practices as plainly
    as we can; it has not been reviewed by a lawyer and should not be treated as a substitute for one.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Cloud Peptides ("we," "us," "our") operates this website, which publishes cited research
    information about peptides and related compounds and, when enabled, sells research materials.
    You can reach us at <a href="mailto:info.order.thecloud@proton.me"
      >info.order.thecloud@proton.me</a
    >, on <a href="https://discord.gg/8pF3AvHgT" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >Discord</a
    >, or at <a href="tel:4434700714">443-470-0714</a>. We do not currently publish a physical
    mailing address.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>We only collect what's actually involved in operating this site today:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Contact form submissions</strong> — the name, email address, and message you submit are
      relayed directly to our inbox by email. We do not currently store contact form submissions in a
      database.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Anti-abuse/verification data</strong> — the contact form (and, once ordering is enabled,
      the order-request form) is protected by Cloudflare Turnstile, a bot-detection challenge, and a short-lived
      cooldown cookie that prevents rapid resubmission from the same browser.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Standard technical data</strong> — like any website, requests to this site pass through
      our hosting/security provider, Cloudflare, which processes technical information (such as IP address)
      to serve the site and to detect abuse (for example, our rate-limiting on forms).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Theme preference</strong> — if you switch to dark mode, that choice is saved in your browser's
      local storage on your device only; it is never sent to us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Shop cart contents</strong> — while browsing the shop, any items you add to a cart are held
      in your browser's local storage on your device only, not on our servers. Ordering itself is not
      currently enabled — see our <a href="/shop-terms">Shop Terms</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Administrative accounts</strong> — our editorial staff sign in through a separate, password-protected
      system to manage published research content. This system is internal and is not available for public
      registration; it is not used to identify or track site visitors.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not currently operate public user accounts, a newsletter, or advertising trackers, and we
    do not sell your personal information to third parties.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to messages sent through the contact form.</li>
    <li>To operate, secure, and improve the website (for example, blocking spam and abuse).</li>
    <li>To fulfill orders and communicate about them, once ordering is enabled.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>This site sets a small number of cookies and browser-local-storage entries:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>A short-lived cookie that enforces a brief cooldown between contact-form submissions.</li>
    <li>
      Session cookies for staff sign-in to the administrative dashboard (not present for ordinary
      visitors).
    </li>
    <li>Your dark/light theme choice and shop cart contents, both stored only in your browser.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>None of these are used for cross-site advertising tracking.</p>

  <h2>Third parties we work with</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosting, content delivery, security, and bot/abuse protection (Turnstile).
    </li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong> — delivers the emails generated by our contact form.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Supabase</strong> — hosts the database that powers our published research content and staff
      authentication.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Each of these providers processes data only as needed to provide their respective service to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Data retention</h2>
  <p>
    Contact-form messages are retained in our email inbox until we delete them. We don't currently
    have a fixed automatic deletion schedule for that inbox — if you'd like a message you sent
    removed, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    Because we don't operate public accounts or a personal-data database for visitors today, there
    isn't a self-service data-access tool to offer yet. If you want to know what we hold about you,
    or want it corrected or deleted, email us and we'll respond directly.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    This site is not directed to, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from, anyone
    under 18.
  </p>

  <h2>International visitors</h2>
  <p>
    We have not yet implemented a specific regional privacy-compliance program (for example, GDPR or
    CCPA-specific processes). If that changes, we will update this policy to describe it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this page as our practices change. The date at the top reflects the most recent
    update.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:info.order.thecloud@proton.me"
      >info.order.thecloud@proton.me</a
    >
    or through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
